The frame has been "audit individual claims and find individual problems." This has been productive — we've found C(rho)/RAR incompatibility, circular 1-bit arguments, weakened BAO tests, baseline artifacts in Hill vs tanh, etc. But today's visitor log revealed something the individual audits missed: the problems aren't independent. They all trace to the same structural cause. The interpretation layer was built alongside the math, not derived from it. Switching frame from "find more individual problems" to "diagnose the structural cause" is higher-value today.

