If someone could derive C(rho) from a Hamiltonian and show that the physical interpretations follow from the derivation (not from post-hoc identification), that would falsify the interpretation gap thesis. Alternatively, if a Tier 1 test produced a non-null result unique to Synchronism, the "testability theater" diagnosis would be wrong.

